course: dictionary
lesson: 15998
title: Vaccinating: protecting people from disease
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Vaccinating means giving someone a vaccine, usually by an injection, to protect them from a disease. Vaccinate is the verb, and vaccinating is the -ing form, used for something happening now. «The nurse is vaccinating the children at school today.»
explain: Use the clues around the word. Nurse, children and school tell you who does it, who it is done to, and where. Those clues show vaccinating is a health job, not cleaning or measuring.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «The nurse is giving the children a vaccine to protect them today.» It still makes sense, so you have understood the word.
fact: Vaccinating means giving someone a vaccine to protect them from a disease.
fact: A vaccine is usually given by an injection, which is a shot with a needle.
fact: «Vaccinating» is also used for animals, as in «vaccinating pets» or «vets are vaccinating farm animals».
fact: A vaccine teaches the body's immune system to recognise a germ, so the body can fight that disease quickly if it meets the germ later.
fact: Vaccinating many people helps protect others too.
exercise: «The nurse is vaccinating the children at school today.» What is the nurse doing? | *Giving the children a vaccine to protect them from a disease | Measuring how tall the children are | Cleaning the children's hands | Taking the children home
exercise: «Vets are vaccinating the farm cows so they stay healthy.» Why are the cows being vaccinated? | To give them a new name | *To protect them from disease | To change their colour | To make them grow bigger
exercise: «Vaccinating many people helps protect others too.» What does this sentence tell you? | Vaccines make people taller | Only one person can ever be protected | *A vaccine can help protect people around the person who is vaccinated | Vaccinating is only for animals
test: What does vaccinating mean? | Washing a cut clean | Feeding a pet at home | *Giving someone a vaccine to protect them from a disease | Taking someone's temperature when they are ill
test: «Vets are vaccinating farm animals.» Who might be doing this? | A baker | *A vet | A footballer | A bus driver
exam: Which phrase is about protecting animals from disease? | reading a story | running in the park | cleaning the classroom | *vaccinating pets
